@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-06-09

Feature: Share Reference Parsing
  "Interprets CLI <ref> arguments as either an object path or a short slug (s/<slug>)."

  Provides:
    - domain.RefKind @source("symbol:RefKind")
    - domain.Ref @source("symbol:Ref")
    - domain.ParseRef @source("symbol:ParseRef")
    - domain.Ref.IsSlug @source("symbol:IsSlug")
    - domain.Ref.IsPath @source("symbol:IsPath")

  Invariants:
    - An s/-prefixed token MUST be parsed as RefKindSlug; all other non-empty tokens are object paths
    - Slug refs MUST include a value after the s/ prefix

  Scenario (happy-path): Object path ref
    Given super/rad/foo.mp3
    When ParseRef runs
    Then Kind is RefKindPath and Value is the full path

  Scenario (happy-path): Slug ref
    Given s/f76
    When ParseRef runs
    Then Kind is RefKindSlug and Value is f76

  Scenario (negative): Empty ref
    Given whitespace only
    When ParseRef runs
    Then it returns an error
